ወይብሉ፡ *ቡሩክ፡ ውእቱ፡ እግዚአ፡ መናፍስት፡ *ወእግዚኦሙ፡ ለነገሥት፡ *ወእግዚኦሙ፡ ለዐዚዛን፡ ወ*እግዚኦሙ፡ ለብዑላን፡ ወ*እግዚአ፡ ስብሐት፡ ወ*እግዚአ፡ ጥበብ።", "translation": {"text": "And they will bless and praise the Lord of spirits[a], and they will say, “Blessed is the Lord of spirits, and the Lord of the kings[c], and the Lord of the mighty, and the Lord of the rich[b], and the Lord of glory, and the Lord of wisdom.”", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "The Ge'ez repeats 'Lord of ...' across each social class and abstract quality; the English keeps that repetition rather than compressing it.", "reason": "cultural_note"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "The phrase rendered 'the rich' may also be understood more broadly as those who possess wealth or property.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "Or 'the Lord of the kings, the Lord of the mighty, the Lord of the rich, the Lord of glory, and the Lord of wisdom.'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 63:3", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ወይበርህ፡ በኵሉ፡ ኅቡእ፡ ኃይልክ፡ ለትውልደ፡ ትውልድ፡ ወስብሐቲከ፡ *ለዓለመ፡ ዓለም፡ ዕሙቅ፡ ውእቱ፡ ኵሉ፡ ኅቡኣት፡ ዚአከ፡ ወኍልቈ፡ አልቦሙ፡ ወጽድቅ፡ ዚአከ፡ ኃሳበ፡ አልቦ።", "language": "Geez", "validation": "current_yaml_comparison", "chapter_file": "sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch63.txt", "pages": [152, 153, 154]}, "current_canonical_source_text": "ወይበርህ፡ በኵሉ፡ ኅቡእ፡ ኃይልክ፡ ለትውልደ፡ ትውልድ፡ ወስብሐቲከ፡ *ለዓለመ፡ ዓለም፡ ዕሙቅ፡ ውእቱ፡ ኵሉ፡ ኅቡኣት፡ ዚአከ፡ ወኍልቈ፡ አልቦሙ፡ ወጽድቅ፡ ዚአከ፡ ኃሳበ፡ አልቦ።", "translation": {"text": "And your power is blessed in every hidden thing throughout all generations[a], and your glory forever and ever. Deep are all your hidden things, and they are without number[c][b]; and your righteousness is beyond reckoning.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "Or 'your secrets' / 'your mysteries' for 'your hidden things.' The Ge'ez is more literally 'your hidden [things].'", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "Or 'your justice' for 'your righteousness.'", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "Or 'And blessed be your hidden power'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 63:4", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ይእዜ፡ አእመርነ፡ ከመ፡ *ንሰብሖ፡ ወንባርኮ፡ ለ*እግዚኦሙ፡ ለነገሥት፡ ወለዘ፡ ይነግሥ፡ ዲበ፡ ኵሎሙ፡ ነገሥት።", "language": "Geez", "validation": "current_yaml_comparison", "chapter_file": "sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch63.txt", "pages": [152, 153, 154]}, "current_canonical_source_text": "ይእዜ፡ አእመርነ፡ ከመ፡ *ንሰብሖ፡ ወንባርኮ፡ ለ*እግዚኦሙ፡ ለነገሥት፡ ወለዘ፡ ይነግሥ፡ ዲበ፡ ኵሎሙ፡ ነገሥት።", "translation": {"text": "Now we know that we ought to praise and bless the Lord of the kings[b][a], and the one who reigns over all the kings.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "Or 'let us praise and bless.' The Ge'ez verbal forms can carry a hortatory or subjunctive sense.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "The title is rendered directly from the Ge'ez as 'Lord of the kings' rather than compressed into the traditional phrase 'King of kings.'", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 63:5", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ወይቤሉ፡ መኑ፡ ወሀበነ፡ ዕረፍተ፡ ከመ፡ *ንሰብሖ፡ ወናአኵቶ፡ ወንእመን፡ ቅድመ፡ ስብሐቲከ።", "language": "Geez", "validation": "current_yaml_comparison", "chapter_file": "sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch63.txt", "pages": [152, 153, 154]}, "current_canonical_source_text": "ወይቤሉ፡ መኑ፡ ወሀበነ፡ ዕረፍተ፡ ከመ፡ *ንሰብሖ፡ ወናአኵቶ፡ ወንእመን፡ ቅድመ፡ ስብሐቲከ።", "translation": {"text": "And they said[a], “Who has given us rest[c][b], that we should praise and thank and believe before your glory?”", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "Or “relief” for “rest.” The noun can denote respite or repose; the context is the lack of any respite under judgment.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "The verb rendered “confess” is difficult in this Ge'ez-only section of the Parables; “acknowledge” is also possible, and some might understand it more weakly as “believe.”", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "Or 'praise and thank and confess'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 63:6", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ይእዜኒ፡ ንስቲተ፡ ዕረፍተ፡ ንትሜነይ፡ ወኢንረክብ፡ *ንሰደድ፡ ወኢንእኅዝ፡ ወብርሃን፡ እምቅድሜነ፡ ኀለፈ፡ ወጽልመት፡ ምኅባሪነ፡ ለዓለመ፡ ዓለም።", "language": "Geez", "validation": "current_yaml_comparison", "chapter_file": "sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch63.txt", "pages": [152, 153, 154]}, "current_canonical_source_text": "ይእዜኒ፡ ንስቲተ፡ ዕረፍተ፡ ንትሜነይ፡ ወኢንረክብ፡ *ንሰደድ፡ ወኢንእኅዝ፡ ወብርሃን፡ እምቅድሜነ፡ ኀለፈ፡ ወጽልመት፡ ምኅባሪነ፡ ለዓለመ፡ ዓለም።", "translation": {"text": "Now we desire a little rest[a], but we do not find it; we are driven away, and we cannot seize it, and the light has passed away from before us[c][b], and darkness will be our dwelling forever and ever.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "The clause rendered 'we cannot seize it' is terse and may mean 'we cannot grasp/lay hold of it,' probably continuing the thought of unattainable rest or security.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "The word rendered 'dwelling' is difficult in this Ge'ez line; 'habitation' is another possible rendering. The sense is that darkness becomes their enduring lot.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "Or 'Now we seek rest for ourselves'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 63:7", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "እስመ፡ በቅድሜሁ፡ *አአመነ፡ ወአሰባሕነ፡ ለስሙ፡ ለእግዚአ፡ መናፈስት፡ [ወአሰባሕናሁ፡ ለእግዚእነ፡] ወተስፋነ፡ ኮነ፡ ዲበ፡ በትረ፡ መንግሥት*ነ፡ ወዲበ፡ ስብሐቲነ፡።", "language": "Geez", "validation": "current_yaml_comparison", "chapter_file": "sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch63.txt", "pages": [152, 153, 154]}, "current_canonical_source_text": "እስመ፡ በቅድሜሁ፡ *አአመነ፡ ወአሰባሕነ፡ ለስሙ፡ ለእግዚአ፡ መናፈስት፡ [ወአሰባሕናሁ፡ ለእግዚእነ፡] ወተስፋነ፡ ኮነ፡ ዲበ፡ በትረ፡ መንግሥት*ነ፡ ወዲበ፡ ስብሐቲነ፡።", "translation": {"text": "For before him we did not believe[a], and we did not praise the name of the Lord of Spirits[a][b], [and we did not praise our Lord,] and our hope was in the scepter of our kingdom and in our glory.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "The bracketed clause 'and we praised our Lord' is uncertain in the supplied witness and may reflect a variant or secondary expansion.", "reason": "textual_variant"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "'Scepter' renders a word that can also mean 'staff' or 'rod'; here the royal sense fits the surrounding confession of misplaced confidence.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "a", "text": "Or 'we believed, and we gave praise to the name of the Lord of Spirits, [and we praised our Lord,]'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 63:8", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ወበዕለተ፡ ስራሕነ፡ ወምንዳቤነ፡ ኢያድኅነነ፡ ወኢንረክብ፡ ዕረፍተ፡ ንእመን፡ እስመ፡ መሃይምን፡ ውእቱ፡ እግዚእነ፡ በኵሉ፡ ምግባሩ፡ ወኵነኔሁ፡ ወጽድቁ፡ ወገጹ፡ ኵነኔ*ሁ፡ ኢይነሥኡ፡።", "language": "Geez", "validation": "current_yaml_comparison", "chapter_file": "sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch63.txt", "pages": [152, 153, 154]}, "current_canonical_source_text": "ወበዕለተ፡ ስራሕነ፡ ወምንዳቤነ፡ ኢያድኅነነ፡ ወኢንረክብ፡ ዕረፍተ፡ ንእመን፡ እስመ፡ መሃይምን፡ ውእቱ፡ እግዚእነ፡ በኵሉ፡ ምግባሩ፡ ወኵነኔሁ፡ ወጽድቁ፡ ወገጹ፡ ኵነኔ*ሁ፡ ኢይነሥኡ፡።", "translation": {"text": "And on the day of our distress and our affliction[a], he will not save us, and we shall find no rest to believe that our Lord is faithful in all his works and in his judgments and his righteousness[c][b], and his judgments show no partiality.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "The clause 'we shall find no rest to believe' is textually and syntactically difficult in the Ge'ez. It may mean 'we shall find no rest in which to trust' or 'we shall find no respite for hope.'", "reason": "alternative_reading"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "Literally, the final clause refers to judgment not 'lifting up the face'—an idiom for showing no favoritism or partiality.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "Or 'in all his works and in his judgments; and his judgment shows no partiality.'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 63:9", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ወነኀልፍ፡ እምገጹ፡ በእንተ፡ ምግባሪነ፡ ወኵሉ፡ ኃጢአትነ፡ በጽድቅ፡ ትኈለቍ።", "language": "Geez", "validation": "current_yaml_comparison", "chapter_file": "sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch63.txt", "pages": [152, 153, 154]}, "current_canonical_source_text": "ወነኀልፍ፡ እምገጹ፡ በእንተ፡ ምግባሪነ፡ ወኵሉ፡ ኃጢአትነ፡ በጽድቅ፡ ትኈለቍ።", "translation": {"text": "And we pass away from before his face because of our deeds[c][b][a], and all our sins are counted in righteousness.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "Or 'from his presence.' The Ge'ez reads literally 'from before his face,' a vivid expression for standing before the divine judge.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "The final clause may also be understood as 'all our sins are counted justly' or 'are taken into account in righteousness.' The Ge'ez is judicial in tone but not fully explicit about the exact nuance.", "reason": "alternative_reading"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "Or 'we pass away from before his face'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 63:10", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ይእዜ፡ ይብልዎሙ፡ ትጸግብ፡ ነፍስነ፡ እምጥየየ፡ ዐመፃ፡ ወኢ*ትከልእ፡ ወረደተነ፡ እምልባ፡ ለክበደ፡ ሲኦል፡።", "language": "Geez", "validation": "current_yaml_comparison", "chapter_file": "sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch63.txt", "pages": [152, 153, 154]}, "current_canonical_source_text": "ይእዜ፡ ይብልዎሙ፡ ትጸግብ፡ ነፍስነ፡ እምጥየየ፡ ዐመፃ፡ ወኢ*ትከልእ፡ ወረደተነ፡ እምልባ፡ ለክበደ፡ ሲኦል፡።", "translation": {"text": "Now they will say to them[a], ‘Our soul has had its fill of unjust gain[d][c][b], but it does not kee